package/fbdoom: new package (NOSDL framebuffer Doom)

fbDOOM (github.com/maximevince/fbDOOM) is the badge's Doom port:
framebuffer rendering, tty keyboard input, no SDL — the only Doom that
works on this fbcon-only NOMMU system (chocolate-doom is BR2_USE_MMU-
blocked, prboom drags the SDL stack). The original package/fbdoom was a
local addition to the reference build tree that was never vendored and
got lost in a tree rebuild — images built from a fresh clone silently
shipped without Doom despite the defconfig's BR2_PACKAGE_FBDOOM=y.
This recreates it: pinned upstream master commit, sha256-hashed, CC
override injecting Buildroot's FLAT target flags (the fbdoom Makefile
assigns CC with '=', and its internal CFLAGS must survive, so CFLAGS
itself is untouched), NOSDL=1, and a 64 KB FLAT stack set via flthdr
at install (Doom recurses; the elf2flt 4 KB default is not survivable,
and FBDOOM_FLAT_STACKSIZE's nested quoting can't pass through the CC
override). Also widens doom-wad's Config.in gate so the shareware WAD
installs alongside (it is upstream, but only selectable with
chocolate-doom/prboom otherwise).

Run: fbdoom -iwad /usr/share/games/doom/doom1.wad -mb 6
(6 MB Z-zone from the patch-0010 NOMMU pool; Backspace exits.)

